@copilot The job failed due to TypeScript errors: Property 'locals' does not exist on type 'RequestEvent'. This affects several lines in the files:

- src/component/locale-links.tsx (line 13)
- src/context/auth.ts (lines 44, 44, 45, 115)
- src/routes/user-menu.tsx (line 19)

Solution:
You need to explicitly define the locals property on your RequestEvent type. If you control its definition, add the locals property like this:

```typescript
interface RequestEvent {
  locals: Record<string, unknown>; // or a more specific type
  // ...other properties
}
```

If importing RequestEvent, you can use type augmentation:

```typescript
declare module "solid-js/web" {
  interface RequestEvent {
    locals: Record<string, unknown>; // or your specific shape
  }
}
```

Apply this wherever RequestEvent is referenced so TypeScript recognizes evt.locals. Also, review event usage in src/routes/user-menu.tsx (line 19) to ensure event.locals follows the same type correction.

With this change, TypeScript errors about missing locals will be resolved, allowing the job to pass.

You can create a custom provider in opencode.json to fix this:
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "poe-fixed": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "Poe (Fixed)",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://api.poe.com/v1",
        "apiKey": "{env:POE_API_KEY}"
      },
      "models": {
        "claude-haiku-4.5": {
          "name": "Claude Haiku 4.5"
        },
        "claude-sonnet-4.6": {
          "name": "Claude Sonnet 4.6"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
Save this to ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json
